# Supabase migrations / RLS

- Every new table in exposed schemas needs RLS enabled and explicit policies.
- Prefer `security_invoker` views; avoid broad `security definer` in `public` unless money RPCs with `SET search_path` + `REVOKE FROM public` + `GRANT TO service_role` (see enterprise-core).
- Never put secrets or service-role keys in migration SQL.
- On this droplet, apply migrations to **self-hosted** Postgres via CLI/`psql` — cloud Supabase MCP cannot reach local Docker DB.
- Do not drop/wipe Hotel OS volumes to fix a migration without explicit user OK.
- Follow [enterprise-core.mdc](enterprise-core.mdc) for tenant isolation; never invent tables like `stays` / `folio_charges` — use `bookings` / `folio_lines`.
